["Here is a basic example of how you can implement this using JavaScript with setTimeout and clearInterval for pausing and resuming data collection. However, note that actual implementation would be more complex due to the variety of real-time sensor streams and messaging systems available. 

```javascript
class SensorDataCollector {
    constructor(sensorStream, messageSystem) {
        this.data = [];
        this.intervalId;
        this.isPaused = false;
        this.sensorStream = sensorStream;
        this.messageSystem = messageSystem;
    }

    start() {
        if (!this.intervalId && !this.isPaused) {
            this.collectData();  // start collection immediately
            this.intervalId = setInterval(() => {
                if (!this.isPaused) {
                    this.collectData();
                }
            }, 1000);  // collect data every second
        } else {
            console.log('Data collection already started');
        }
    }

    pause() {
        this.isPaused = true;
    }

    resume() {
        this.isPaused = false;
    }

    stop() {
        clearInterval(this.intervalId);
        this.intervalId = null;
        this.messageSystem.sendMessage('Data collection stopped');
    }

    collectData() {
        try {
            const dataPoint = this.sensorStream.getNext();  // consider async/await for real-world scenarios
            if (dataPoint) {
                this.data.push(dataPoint);
            }
        } catch (error) {
            console.log('Error collecting data', error);
            this.stop();
        } finally {
            setTimeout(() => { // simulate random delay between stops
                if (!this.isPaused && Math.random() < 0.1) {  // 10% chance to stop
                    this.stop();
                }
            }, Math.floor(Math.random() * 5000));  // up to 5 seconds delay
        }
    }
}
```
Please consider, that `sensorStream` and `messageSystem` are objects with methods `getNext()` (that fetches data from the sensor stream) and `sendMessage(msg)` (that sends a message through messaging system), these need to be implemented according to specific sensor streams and messaging systems.

This example focuses on performance optimization by pausing and resuming data collection, but does not take into account memory management issues such as excessive resource consumption in the long run. For production use, you would want to implement more sophisticated handling of data storage (e.g., discarding old or unnecessary data), error recovery measures for sensor stream failures, and optimizations for messaging system performance.
