using System;
using System.IO;
using System.IO.Compression;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Threading;

public class FileCache<T> where T : Stream, new()
{
    private readonly Dictionary<string, CacheItem> cache = new Dictionary<string, CacheItem>();
    private static readonly ReaderWriterLockSlim lock_ = new ReaderWriterLockSlim();

    public delegate Stream Decompressor(Stream input);
    public Decompressor decompressor;

    public class CacheItem
    {
        public T data;
        public DateTime lastAccessed;
    }

    public FileCache() : this((input) => new GZipStream(input, CompressionMode.Decompress)) {}

    public FileCache(Decompressor decompressor)
    {
        this.decompressor = decompressor;
    }

    public T LoadFile(string filePath)
    {
        lock_.EnterUpgradeableLock();
        try
        {
            if (!cache.ContainsKey(filePath) || (DateTime.Now - cache[filePath].lastAccessed).TotalMinutes > 5) // LRU Cache expiration period can be adjusted as per your requirement.
            {
                lock_.EnterWriteLock();
                try
                {
                    using (FileStream compressedFile = File.Open(filePath, FileMode.Open))
                    using (var decompressedFile = decompressor(compressedFile))
                    {
                        var dataStructure = new T();
                        decompressedFile.CopyTo(dataStructure);
                        dataStructure.Position = 0; // Reset to the beginning of the stream.

                        if (cache.ContainsKey(filePath)) cache[filePath].data = dataStructure;
                        else cache.Add(filePath, new CacheItem { data = dataStructure });
                    }
                }
                finally
                {
                    lock_.ExitWriteLock();
                }
            }

            cache[filePath].lastAccessed = DateTime.Now; // update last access time.
            return cache[filePath].data;
        }
        finally
        {
            lock_.ExitUpgradeableLock();
        }
    }
}
```
In this class, we have a LRU cache which is implemented with a `Dictionary`. Each entry in the dictionary corresponds to an item in the cache and includes the data (of your custom type) and the last access time of that file. We use ReaderWriterLockSlim to ensure thread-safety for concurrent accesses.

The constructor allows you to provide a custom decompressor function, so you can easily switch between different compression formats without changing the rest of the code. 

This class could be used in the following way:
```csharp
var cache = new FileCache<MemoryStream>(); // for example, if your data is stored in MemoryStream
using (var stream = cache.LoadFile("path-to-file"))
{
    // do something with the loaded file
}
```
The `using` statement ensures that the stream gets properly disposed and returned to the pool of available streams. Note that you should replace the `MemoryStream` with your actual custom type as necessary. 

This implementation provides a simple, flexible, efficient solution for this problem while considering real-world factors. However, there are always areas for improvement based on specific use cases or requirements. For example, you might need to add error handling, logging, or advanced features like cache eviction policies. But the basic approach should work in most scenarios.
']

['```java
import java.io.*;
import java.util.logging.Logger;

public class ObjectDeserializer {
    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(ObjectDeserializer.class.getName());

    public static <T> T deserialize(byte[] data, Class<T> expectedClass, int expectedVersion) throws RuntimeException {
        ByteArrayInputStream byteInStream;
        ObjectInputStream objInStream = null;

        try {
            byteInStream = new ByteArrayInputStream(data);
            objInStream = new ObjectInputStream(byteInStream);

            T object = expectedClass.cast(objInStream.readObject());

            if (object instanceof Versioned && ((Versioned) object).getVersion() != expectedVersion) {
                logger.severe("Deserialized data version does not match the expected version.");
                throw new RuntimeException("Invalid serialized data: version mismatch");
            }

            return object;
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            logger.severe("Failed to deserialize data: " + e.getMessage());
            throw new RuntimeException("Failed to deserialize data", e);
        } finally {
            if (objInStream != null) {
                try {
                    objInStream.close();
                } catch (IOException e) {
                    logger.warning("Failed to close ObjectInputStream: " + e.getMessage());
                }
            }
        }
    }

    interface Versioned {
        int getVersion();
    }
}
```

This code uses Java's built-in serialization mechanism to deserialize a byte array into an object of the specified class. It logs error messages and throws exceptions if any IO or ClassNotFoundException occurs during the process, or if the version number of the deserialized object doesn't match the expected value. It also ensures that ObjectInputStream is closed after use to prevent resource leaks. Note that this code assumes that all objects being serialized implement the Versioned interface and provide a getVersion method for checking their versions against an expected value.
