['Here is a solution in Java using parallel streams from the java 8 version which allows for fast computation with large lists by taking advantage of multi-core CPUs if available. This uses MD5 as an example but you could change it to SHA, etc depending on your needs. The method also handles exceptions and will calculate the MD5 hash in a lazy way to avoid excessive memory usage:

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.security.*;
import java.util.*;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.util.stream.*;
import static java.util.function.Function.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> filePaths = Arrays.asList("/path/to/file1", "/path/to/file2");
        Map<String, String> md5Hashes = computeMD5HashesInParallel(filePaths);
    }

    public static Map<String, String> computeMD5HashesInParallel(List<String> filePaths) {
        return filePaths.parallelStream()
                .collect(Collectors.toConcurrentMap(identity(), Main::md5Hash));
    }

    private static String md5Hash(String path) {
        try (InputStream is = Files.newInputStream(Paths.get(path))) {
            MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("MD5");
            byte[] buffer = new byte[1024];
            int read;
            while ((read = is.read(buffer)) != -1) {
                md.update(buffer, 0, read);
            }
            return toHexString(md.digest());
        } catch (IOException | NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
            throw new UncheckedIOException(e);
        }
    }

    private static String toHexString(byte[] bytes) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (byte b : bytes) {
            sb.append(String.format("%02x", b));
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }
}
```

This solution uses `Files.newInputStream` to read the file in a lazy manner and calculates the MD5 hash only when needed (i.e., during `collect(Collectors.toConcurrentMap)`). It also catches potential exceptions as unchecked so that it can be handled by caller if necessary.
']

