In the function above, we've created a struct named "record" to store an integer and a string of length RECORD_SIZE. We allocate memory for arrays for long ints (offsetValues), integers (keys), and records based on the input size. We then fill each record with random data and copy strings from the input array into the char array inside the struct. The function returns 0 if allocation was successful, and -1 otherwise. It also checks if any individual string is too long before filling anything in to prevent buffer overflows.
